Coaches can split one session time(slot) aounsts multiple students


~~Q: how many students max are allowed to split a lesson. 
Let the coach decide this? or hard code?~~ *Answered: default 1, max 2 (ADR-026 P1).*


Decided 2026-10-07:

Coach: when the coach makes the schedule they set how many skaters can split each lesson (per block).
  Default value is 1 (private). Default max is 2. The max might be raised later.

Client booking:
  The client does not see how many skaters can share a lesson.
  A "share this lesson" box only shows on times whose block allows 2 or more.
  Only 1 skater code can be entered in the box.
  Note in the box: skater 2's family must accept before skater 2 can join the lesson.
  On entering a skater code, the system checks the skater exists and shows first name and last initial (e.g. Mia R.).
  The booking only continues once skater 2 is validated as existing.

Coach acceptance:
  A student must always be accepted by the coach before any lessons are booked for that student.
  A client can invite a skater the coach hasn't accepted, but nothing is booked for skater 2 until the coach accepts them.
  If the coach does not accept skater 2 (or doesn't act before the lesson), the lesson proceeds as a private lesson.

Invitation (changed 2026-10-07):
  When a family splits a lesson, an email is sent to family B straight away.
  If skater B is already the coach's student, the email is a normal invite to accept or decline.
  If skater B is not part of that coach, the email says something like:
    "Coach XXX needs to accept you first. By clicking the link below you agree to be added to Coach XXX's roster of students."
  The link opens a confirmation page. Family B must sign in and confirm on the page.
  The confirmation page shows skater B any conflicting bookings they would have. They can go ahead or cancel.
  If they go ahead, the request follows the same flow as if they had entered the coach code at sign up.
  When the coach accepts skater B, skater B joins the lesson automatically.
  Before writing anything, the job checks that the lesson slot still exists and hasn't happened yet.
    *Per ADR-026 d5: done by the coach's Accept itself, which also checks there's room and that the booking named this skater.*
  If those aren't true it does nothing, and family B is notified that the booking didn't happen.
  Recurring booking: the code shares every lesson in the series.
  Sibling (same family): just booked, no confirmation needed (still needs coach acceptance first).

See docs/adr/ADR-026-shared-lessons-by-invitation.md.
